# TPL -> SPL -> FIT chain, layered ON TOP of a single-file -libre defconfig:
#
#   make libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig tpl-spl-chain.config olddefconfig
#   make libretech-cc_libre_defconfig    tpl-spl-chain.config olddefconfig
#
# and with the MMC boot source as well:
#
#   make libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig tpl-spl-chain.config tpl-mmc.config \
#        olddefconfig
#
# The base is the SHIPPING open-chain defconfig -- the one LBS names in
# configs/aml-s905x-cc{,-v2}-libre and the one every hardware result on this
# board was measured from.  It is NOT libretech-cc_v2_defconfig +
# spl-usb.config: that stack predates the DDR4 2 GB map, the four-lane
# memtest, the EL3 raise, the DMC SEC AXI word, the 0x0c000000 FIT staging
# address and the size repair, so building the chain on it would test a
# different SPL than the one that boots.
#
# The base defconfig alone still builds the shipping single-stage SPL -- the one
# that runs from SRAM, owns DDR + the DWC2 server and is 40075 B (DDR4) /
# 37427 B (DDR3) against the 0xb000 ceiling.  Nothing here is allowed to change
# that binary; every symbol below only applies when this fragment is applied.
#
# What this fragment does is move the SPL phase out of SRAM.  TPL keeps the
# geometry the single stage had (0xd9001000, 0xb000, SRAM stack) because it is
# now the stage in that role; SPL is relinked into DRAM, loses the ceiling, and
# loses the receive path -- the DWC2 session belongs entirely to TPL and is torn
# down before the branch.
# --- TPL: the SRAM stage the BootROM loads (T0 of the chain) ---
# Geometry is the SPL's old geometry: same load address, same 0xb000 ceiling,
# same stack.  What changes is that this stage stops being the last one.
# These lived in spl-usb.config until the chain got its own recipe; they are
# chain-only symbols and belong with the chain.
CONFIG_TPL=y
CONFIG_TPL_TEXT_BASE=0xd9001000
CONFIG_TPL_MAX_SIZE=0xb000
CONFIG_TPL_SIZE_LIMIT=0xb000
CONFIG_TPL_HAVE_INIT_STACK=y
CONFIG_TPL_STACK=0xd900ff00
CONFIG_TPL_SYS_MALLOC_SIMPLE=y
CONFIG_TPL_LIBCOMMON_SUPPORT=y	# panic() and friends
CONFIG_TPL_LIBGENERIC_SUPPORT=y	# udelay() via lib/
# The one thing the single stage could not afford and this one can.
#
# spl-usb.config turns SPL_SERIAL off and explains at length that the stage is
# still NOT silent, because common/console.o falls through to the DEBUG_UART
# printch().  That reasoning holds only while common/console.o is LINKED, and
# common/Makefile keys it on CONFIG_$(PHASE_)SERIAL -- so with TPL_SERIAL off
# the TPL has no console.o at all and every printf() in dram-gx.c and
# meson_spl_selfcheck() goes nowhere.  Measured on hardware 2026-08-12: the TPL
# emitted "SPL 1 2 4 5 USB FIT JMP" (the bare-metal early_puts breadcrumbs) and
# not one DDR line, so "DDR: 2048 MB ... memtest OK to 0x7fffffff" and
# "SELFCHK: ..." -- the two statements this stage exists to make about DRAM --
# were unobservable, and the memtest verdict could only be INFERRED from
# dram_init() returning 0.
#
# The 1056 B this costs is why the single stage cannot have it (it has 4981 B
# of headroom on DDR4 and 29 B was the DDR3 margin before ee3e4bc09e5).  TPL
# has ~28 KB spare, which is precisely the headroom the split was built to
# create.  Spend a twentieth of it on being able to read the DRAM result.
CONFIG_TPL_SERIAL=y
# T1: the SRAM stage owns the receive path -- DDR init, DWC2 server, handoff
# block.
CONFIG_TPL_MESON_USB_BOOT=y

CONFIG_MESON_GX_XPL_CHAIN=y
CONFIG_MESON_GX_SPL_ENTRY=0x08000000

# Clear of every address the FIT path uses: BL33 0x01000000, SCP 0x013c0000,
# BL31 0x05100000 -- or, under CONFIG_MESON_GX_LIBRE_SECURE_LAYOUT, BL33
# 0x04000000, SCP 0x00001000, BL31 0x00100000, all of which 0x08000000 also
# clears -- and the FIT staging address (CONFIG_SPL_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS) the board
# defconfig sets: 0x0c000000 on libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig since
# 1663e862b56, 0x02000000 on libretech-cc_libre_defconfig since 584916c96db.
# 0x08000000 sits between the two and clears both: the DDR3 board stages the
# FIT 96 MiB below it and the DDR4 board 64 MiB above it, and the DRAM stage
# itself is ~33 KiB (~37 KiB if CONFIG_SPL_LZMA is added).
#
# Do not confuse either with MESON_SPL_FIT_BUFFER_ADDR 0x05000000 (spl.c), the
# FIT WORKING buffer under MESON_GX_LIBRE_SECURE_LAYOUT.  Different address,
# different job -- and it is pinned rather than derived precisely so it cannot
# drift onto 0x08000000 and have the DRAM stage stage a FIT on top of itself.
#
# Must equal MESON_GX_SPL_ENTRY; the DRAM stage checks the pair through the
# handoff block rather than hanging.
CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE=0x08000000

# No amlimage ceiling out here -- that is the entire point of the split.  What
# is left is a linker-region bound whose VALUE is borrowed rather than chosen:
# include/config_fallbacks.h enforces SPL_PAD_TO >= SPL_MAX_SIZE, so 0x1fe00 is
# simply the largest bound this check will accept.
#
# It is NOT the bound that actually binds.  The DRAM stage is placed in the
# image between the signed SRAM stage and the FIT, so its real ceiling is
# MESON_GX_SPL_OFFSET (0xc000) -> MESON_GX_FIT_OFFSET (0x1fe00) = 0x13e00,
# 81408 B.  Budget against that, not against SPL_MAX_SIZE.  (The FIT offset
# having its own symbol was once listed here as open plumbing; it is
# MESON_GX_FIT_OFFSET and it is done.)
CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE=0x1fe00
CONFIG_SPL_SIZE_LIMIT=0x0

# A compressed FIT is NOT enabled here, deliberately.  CONFIG_SPL_LZMA changes
# what the FIT CONTAINS, and this file is shared, so setting it here would move
# every target that includes it onto a boot path measured on none of them.  It
# belongs in the consuming target's own defconfig -- see
# amlogic/software/boot/design/boot-chain-policy.md section 3b, "a target is ONE
# defconfig".  What this fragment provides is the PRECONDITION: an SPL that runs
# from DRAM and can therefore afford a decompressor at all (in SRAM it overflows
# .sram by 1288 B even size-optimised).
#
# This file is itself a leftover.  The ten Amlogic targets that used to stack
# fragments were folded into real defconfigs in fa26ab4aa27; what keeps this one
# alive is the three aml-s905x-cc-libre-eye* bench targets, which cannot be
# converted yet because they reference dram-libretech-cc-2rank.config, a file
# that does not exist on this branch.  Fold them and delete this.

# SPL never touches the DWC2: TPL owns the whole session and stops the device
# before jumping.  Carrying a live enumerated link across the stage boundary is
# the one thing this stack must not do.
# CONFIG_SPL_MESON_USB_BOOT is not set

# BSS and stack stay at their SRAM addresses.  arch/arm/cpu/armv8/u-boot-spl.lds
# reads CONFIG_SPL_BSS_START_ADDR in BOTH phases (it is not phase-prefixed), so
# moving it would move the TPL BSS too -- into DRAM, which does not exist when
# TPL zeroes it.  SRAM is free by the time the DRAM stage runs: TPL is done with
# it, and the 0xd900c000-c240 breadcrumb window is below both.
